{
  "info": {
    "name": "Playlist API",
    "description": "Coleccion de la API de playlists (Spring Boot). Ejecutala en orden: cada carpeta depende de la anterior.\n\nAntes de empezar: arranca el backend (perfil dev) y revisa las variables de la coleccion: baseUrl, username, password.\nEl usuario demo/Demo1234! es una credencial de demostracion que solo existe en el perfil dev.\n\nSeguridad: el JWT va en la cookie HttpOnly access_token y la proteccion CSRF exige la cabecera X-XSRF-TOKEN con el valor de la cookie XSRF-TOKEN. Los scripts de la coleccion guardan el token tras cada respuesta (variable xsrfToken) y lo agregan solos a POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE.\nPostman debe tener activado el manejo automatico de cookies (por defecto lo esta).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "username",
      "value": "demo"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Demo1234!"
    },
    {
      "key": "listName",
      "value": "ListaDemo"
    },
    {
      "key": "emptyListName",
      "value": "ListaVacia"
    },
    {
      "key": "xsrfToken",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const xsrf = pm.cookies.get(\"XSRF-TOKEN\");",
          "if (xsrf) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"xsrfToken\", xsrf); }"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const unsafe = [\"POST\", \"PUT\", \"PATCH\", \"DELETE\"];",
          "const token = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"xsrfToken\");",
          "if (unsafe.includes(pm.request.method) && token && !pm.request.headers.has(\"X-XSRF-TOKEN\")) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.add({ key: \"X-XSRF-TOKEN\", value: token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 - Preparacion (CSRF)",
      "description": "Obtiene la cookie XSRF-TOKEN. El backend la emite en cualquier peticion, aun sin sesion.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/me sin sesion -> 401 y cookie XSRF-TOKEN",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 401\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test(\"El backend emite la cookie XSRF-TOKEN\", () => pm.expect(pm.cookies.get(\"XSRF-TOKEN\")).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty);",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Cuerpo de error uniforme\", () => pm.expect(body.codigo).to.eql(\"UNAUTHORIZED\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "01 - Autenticacion",
      "description": "El JWT viaja en la cookie HttpOnly access_token (Postman la guarda sola). El token nunca va en el cuerpo.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /auth/login -> 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Cuerpo con username y expiresAt, sin token\", () => { pm.expect(body.username).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"username\")); pm.expect(body.expiresAt).to.be.a(\"string\"); pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"token\"); pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"access_token\"); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /auth/login con credenciales malas -> 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 401\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"INVALID_CREDENTIALS\", () => pm.expect(body.codigo).to.eql(\"INVALID_CREDENTIALS\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"incorrecta\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/me con sesion -> 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Devuelve el usuario y la expiracion\", () => { pm.expect(body.username).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"username\")); pm.expect(body.expiresAt).to.be.a(\"string\"); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
